r A's Stop) also counts as only when processed (queued-message arrival rule, host binding table); a way passes only when its B produced exactly one UserPromptSubmit line (a second line with another `turn_id` would mint a second turn), whose `turn_id` differs from A's and from every other B's, because codex's nonce is `turn_id` (host binding table) and a shared `turn_id` would merge B into A's turn (when a way fires only when processed, P0.2 also records whether the transcript at the payload's `transcript_path` records the enqueue, with its observed payload, for the operator). The codex row fails or is unavailable when run 1 records no UserPromptSubmit line or a payload without `session_id` or `turn_id`, when a way's B, the `codex queue` one included, produces no UserPromptSubmit line, more than one, or one that shares a `turn_id`, or when run 2 cannot be performed; a failed or unavailable codex row, or a result of only when processed for any way, stops P0 and the operator is shown the receipt, because every HV reviewer must persist its own turn through the Codex plugin (host binding table, codex), so every codex arrival path ends either verified or decided by the operator. Afterwards P0.2 copies `observed.jsonl` and run 1's stdout, redacted by the receipt rule of the hostile validation protocol, to `docs/receipts/p0/codex-hook-observer-<utc>.jsonl` and `docs/receipts/p0/codex-hook-probe-exec-<utc>.jsonl`, stops the private app server, signs the probe home out (`env CODEX_HOME=<home> codex logout`), deletes `/tmp/qbrain-p02-codex-<utc>/` (the directory it created), and confirms that `~/.codex/config.toml` still has the recorded SHA-256 and that no file under `~/.codex` contains the probe directory's path (otherwise it stops and shows the operator what changed), so the probe leaves no Codex setting, credential, or path-bearing record in the operator's Codex home; the UserPromptSubmit lines of `codex-hook-observer-<utc>.jsonl` are the recorded codex event payloads that