    "8. Create TODOs with `workflow.todo.create` (section SessionLog, priority high, FR/TR arrays, dependsOn): MCP-SESSIONTURN-001..009 (A1..A9), MCP-SESSIONREVIEW-001..011 (S1..S11). Chain: A1 and A2 roots; A3 depends on A1; A4 on A1, A3 (its RED consumes A3's arrival bridge, queue, and minted turns); A5 on A1, A4; A6 on A1, A3, A4 (its RED uses A3's `MCP_PLUGIN_HOOK_INVOCATION=1` and `SessionTurnIntegrity.Tests.ps1` and A4's per-turn store); A7 on A3, A4, A5, A6 (it consumes A5's outcome mapping and A6's model-evidence counters and hook-invocation exclusion); A8 on A1; A9 on A2..A8; S1 on A9; S2 on S1; S3 on S2; S4 on S3; S5 on S4; S6 on S5; S7 on S2, S5; S8 on S6, S7; S9 on S5, S6, S7, S8 (C12: the S6 REPL release carrying `recordReview` and lossless scores precedes the Node host pins; S9 re-syncs the same 1.120.0 version S8 writes); S10 on S6, S7, S8, S9; S11 on S10. Append PlanningDecision checkpoints for every locked decision and rejected alternative. Write each host's D6/D7 capability disposition from its P0.2 receipt into `docs/AGENT-PLUGIN-FEATURE-MATRIX.md` (one row per plugin and feature with the receipt; P0.2 itself stays read-only). For each queue or enqueue event that P0.2 recorded on a host without a specified adapter, also create one follow-up TODO (canonical id assigned at creation; it carries the P0.2 receipt, the observed payload, and the host's feature-matrix row, and proposes that adapter for operator approval); none of them is a dependency of A1-S11.",
    "9. Gate P0: G5 as defined in the BDPv4 contract, including the phase-exit strict TR/TEST run (judged against the baseline findings P0.3 recorded) and the scoped use-case gate (operator D3): `client.UseCases.GetCoverageAsync` lists none of the catalog FRs in `functionalRequirementsWithoutRealizesUseCase` (baseline 2026-10-09T03:12Z: 0 use cases, all 352 FRs unlinked; the pre-existing FRs are out of scope by D3); `./build.ps1 ValidateConfig`; the baseline-green run of `SessionLogServiceReplaceDeleteTests` (TDD AC allocation) with zero failures and zero skips; HV-P0 by Codex gpt-6-sol xhigh against the pushed P0 branch head (claims: the 2026-10-10 amendment applied as ruled (every Build.Tests run is the Build.Tests infrastructure step, never G1 or G2; no FR AC or TEST record cites a Build.Tests case; Nuke behavior only in TR-MCP-NUKE-003 and TR-MCP-NUKE-004, mapped only to the build-tooling FR FR-MCP-BUILD-001, with no TEST record; npm lockfiles changed only through npm), ids in store and docs, ACs testable, UCs linked, interfaces documented, dependsOn valid, defect receipts reproducible, and every P0.2 row recorded with its receipt, including the codex observer receipts, the removal of the probe home, and the unchanged SHA-256 of `~/.codex/config.toml`). New TODOs are created `Planned` (`TodoExecutionService.cs:1031`); no slice TODO leaves Planned before HV-P0 AGREE.",
    "## Requirements catalog",
    "AC ids use `<REQID>-AC###`, the format of the SESSIONLIFE family this plan updates (e.g. `FR-MCP-SESSIONLIFE-001-AC004`). New ACs on existing requirements keep that requirement's existing AC format (`ac-N` for FR-SUPPORT-*, SESSIONLOGSAN, TRIAGESTORE, PLUGININT); requirements that today carry only inline prose ACs get structured `<REQID>-AC###` ACs. In the allocation lists, shorthand `SESSIONTURN-004-001` means `FR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-004-AC001`. The bracket after each AC names the slice whose RED test first covers it; \"+\" lists later slices that extend coverage on another surface. Each AC is verified by the TEST listed under its TR, except a TR AC that names Build.Tests cases as its evidence (TR-MCP-CLEARSESSION-001-AC002 and every AC of TR-MCP-NUKE-003 and TR-MCP-NUKE-004): those cases, run in the Build.Tests infrastructure step (BDPv4 contract), verify it, and no FR AC or TEST record in this catalog cites a Build.Tests case. Nuke behavior lives only in the Nuke TRs (here TR-MCP-NUKE-003 and TR-MCP-NUKE-004), which are implementation detail of the build-tooling FR FR-MCP-BUILD-001 \"Tooling for repeatable builds\" and have no TEST record (operator, 2026-10-10: \"NUKE is only accountable through TR.\"; the decision \"Separate Nuke-only TRs\"; and \"FR: Project will provide tooling for repeatable builds.\" / \"Now, the TR are implementation detail of the FR.\"); every TR that maps to an application FR keeps only application ACs. FR-MCP-BUILD-001 is tested by running `./build.ps1 -WhatIf` (TR-MCP-NUKE-005, TODO PLAN-BUILDWHATIF-001, outside this plan). Each new TEST record carries exactly the three ACs of the rule under \"New testing requirements\".",
