    "## Phase A: correct, independent turn logging (ships first)",
    "A1 MCP-SESSIONTURN-001 Server per-turn submit outcomes and ingress mint. Precondition met: Codex ACKed the C3 change in `MEMORY-PROCESS-007` at 21:51:50Z. Reqs SESSIONTURN-004 (server ACs), SESSIONTURN-001 (server mint ACs). Contract: `ISessionLogService.SubmitWithOutcomesAsync` (SubmitAsync delegates), outcome DTOs, seam `ISessionLogTurnUpsertGuard`; seam `ISessionLogRequestIdMinter.Mint(utcNow)` (format `req-<yyyyMMddTHHmmssZ>-<8 hex>`); `ISessionLogService.MintTurnAsync`; the mint route, `SessionLogMintTurnRequest`, client `MintTurnAsync` with `McpClientJsonContext` registration, REPL `workflow.sessionlog.mintTurn`; `SessionLogTurnEntity.IngressNonce` with the unique filtered index and migration `<utc>_AddSessionLogTurnIngressNonce` per provider (same `dotnet ef migrations add` procedure as S3). RED: `SessionLogSubmitOutcomeTests` (incl. d3a5 repro `InProgressOntoCanceledTurn_ReportsSkippedTerminal_ActionsRemainZero`, `IdenticalResubmit_ReportsMergedNoChange`, `DuplicateRequestIdInOneSubmission_LastWins_OneOutcome`, `NoSkippedDuplicateOutcome_OnRestMcpClientRepl`), `SessionLogTerminalTurnGuardContractTests` (CT), `SessionLogIngressMintTests` (mint format, same nonce returns same requestId, two nonces with identical prompt text return two requestIds, concurrent same-nonce mints yield one turn (`MintRace_SameNonce_NonceIndexViolation_ReturnsExistingId`), a forced requestId-index violation generates a new id (`MintRace_RequestIdIndexViolation_RetriesNewId`) five collisions then success on the sixth attempt (`MintRace_FiveCollisions_SixthAttemptSucceeds`), and six collisions return HTTP 500 with the final detail code `mint_collision_exhausted` (`MintRace_SixCollisions_500FinalDetailCode`), each on SQLite, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server, supplied requestId unchanged; a requestId-index violation never merges into another turn (`MinterCollision_ReturnsDistinctId`, `MintCollision_ConcurrentCrossSession_DistinctIds`, each on SQLite, PostgreSQL, and SQL Server); a same-nonce mint for a terminal turn returns `merged` with its `storedStatus` and leaves the status unchanged (`Mint_SameNonceTerminalTurn_MergedNotReopened`)), `SessionLogRequestIdMinterContractTests` (CT), migration Up/Down tests per provider, `SessionLogControllerMintTests` (201, 200 merged, 400 nonce and planFile/todoId, 404 with detail code `session_not_open` for an unopened session, `/mcpserver` alias), `SessionLogClientMintTests` (`MockHttpHandler`), `McpToolSurfaceHasNoMintToolTests` (no `[McpServerTool]` exposes the mint), REPL mint dispatch test, controller/MCP/client/REPL/decorator forwarding tests (the plugin wrapper refusal of `mintTurn` is an A3 case). Mocks-green: NSubstitute guard and minter. Real: `UpsertTurns` 1590-1630 returns outcomes, decorators, controller 71-86, MCP tool, `McpClientJsonContext`, `SessionLogModels.cs:396-425`, REPL persistence, `MintTurnAsync` behind the mint route. Gates G1, G2, G3 (IntegrationTests, SessionLog.Validation, `./build.ps1 MigrationIntegrationTests --skip InstallTestDependencies` against the P0.1 PostgreSQL and SQL Server endpoints), G5.",
    "A2 MCP-SESSIONTURN-002 Hook registration integrity (plugin repo). Reqs SESSIONTURN-001 (validator/installer ACs). Contract: validator JSON adds `duplicate`/`repaired`, `duplicateHooks`, `pluginEnabled`, `pluginKey`; `Test-PluginEnabled` handles the `enabledPlugins` map via `known_marketplaces.json`; `Get-DuplicateHookCommands`; installer adds no bridge hooks when the plugin covers the event and removes managed duplicates (with backup). RED: `tests/ClaudeHookWiring.Tests.ps1` (observed settings shape reports `duplicate`, CheckOnly read-only, repair keeps user hooks, installer behavior). Gates G6, G2. Operator action before HV-A, with operator approval once A2's gates are green: run the validator repair and restart Claude Code, recording a live receipt; it is repeated after the phase merge only if the merged validator differs.",
    "A3 MCP-SESSIONTURN-003 Ingress mint and system-event classifier (plugin). Reqs SESSIONTURN-001 (plugin mint ACs), -002. Contract: the atomic `turn-state.yaml` queue, delivery, and write-target writer used by the bridge and by the prompt hook on hosts without a bridge (a prompt-hook mint is delivered at once and becomes the host session's write target, TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-001 AC-005 and AC-006; A4 adds the invocation binding to that write target and the other authorized writers, TR-MCP-SESSIONTURN-003 AC-006/007), `Test-PluginPromptIsSystemEvent` with the subagent markers (`agent_id`, `subagentType`, `MCP_SUBAGENT_ID`/`GROK_SUBAGENT_ID`), `Get-PluginIngressNonce` with the per-host nonce sources of the host binding table (codex `turn_id`, grok and grok-bot `promptId`, copilot `cp-`; classic cline's `cl-` is Node, A8), `Invoke-PluginIngressMint`, `Start-PluginArrivalBridge` and its launch from the SessionStart hook, `Sync-PluginArrivalLog`, `Enter/Exit-PluginTurnOpenLock`, `MCP_PLUGIN_HOOK_INVOCATION=1` for hook-originated verbs; the prompt-text dedupe in the current hook is deleted. A3/A4 split rule: A3's cases assert bridge and mint state only (queue entries, `unsupportedSince`, cursor, mint calls); each case's verb-side assertion (refusal with `turn_logging_unsupported` or `request_unknown`, zero writes, zero wrong-turn writes, idle revival) runs in A4 with the same fixture under the same case name, and the failsafe capture of an already open turn's writes runs in A7. The alias-journal cases use synthetic queued records for the journal and the mint; the rebind of real queued writes through the persist path and the \"no lost write\" assertion are the A5 extension. Per-host mint cases follow the P0.2 gating rule. RED: new `SessionTurnIntegrity.Tests.ps1` (mocked server: one delivery retried three times and a failsafe replay of its mint open one turn (`IngressMint_RetryAndFailsafeReplay_OneTurn`); for each PowerShell host whose prompt hook mints with a per-message id nonce (codex, grok, grok-bot; claude-code and claude-cowork mint only through the bridge) two independent `Start-Job` hook processes fed the same recorded payload open one turn (`IngressMint_TwoHookProcessesOneEvent_OneTurn_PerMessageIdHosts`; for a host whose P0.2 row did not pass, `Grok_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites`, `GrokBot_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites`, or `Copilot_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites` instead), while for copilot, whose nonce has no per-message id, a second invocation with the same payload after the first has minted mints nothing and fails the host session closed (`Copilot_SamePromptDifferentTimestamp_TwoMints`, `Copilot_EqualFieldsSecondInvocation_FailsClosed_NoSecondMint`, `Copilot_MintRetryAndFailsafeReplay_ReuseNonce_NoFailClose`), and two payloads that differ only in the event id or timestamp open two turns; two messages with identical text open two turns (`IngressMint_IdenticalTextTwoEvents_TwoTurns`); failsafe replay of a mint returns the same requestId; outage opens `pending-<nonce>` and the drain journals the alias in `sessions/<key>/aliases.yaml`, run with synthetic queued records (crash before the journal replace, after it and before the record rewrite, and mid-rewrite each end with one mint and the synthetic records intact: `AliasJournal_CrashBoundaries_OneMintNoLostWrite`, extended in A5 with real queued writes; a read by either id resolves the same turn: `AliasJournal_ResolveEitherId_SameTurn`; replay reapplies a journaled alias without minting: `AliasJournal_Replay_NoReMint`); system events (including `agent_id` and `subagentType` payloads, and deliveries with `MCP_SUBAGENT_ID` or `GROK_SUBAGENT_ID` set) open nothing, call no mint, and report `system-event-skipped` (`SystemEvents_HookReportsSkipped_NoMint`, `SystemEvents_SubagentEnvMarkers_NoMint`), and a `<task-notification>` prompt never opens a phantom turn (`PromptHook_TaskNotification_NoPhantomTurn`); a hook-originated `mintTurn` without `MCP_PLUGIN_HOOK_INVOCATION=1` is refused by the plugin wrapper with `mint_requires_host_ingress` (`MintVerb_WithoutHookInvocation_RefusedMintRequiresHostIngress`); a payload missing its host row's nonce field reports `turn-open-failed` with `nonce_source_missing`, invents no nonce, and writes the failsafe diagnostic (`NonceSourceMissing_TurnOpenFailed_FailsafeDiagnostic`); slash command opens; contended lock reports `turn-open-contended` and calls no mint (`ContendedTurnOpenLock_ReportsTurnOpenContended_NoMint`); failed open retried; arrival bridge on a fixture transcript: an `enqueue` line mints once, a restart resumes from the stored offset without re-minting,  bridge cases on synthetic fixtures (run in both P0.2 branches), the real captured Claude Code prompt-form fixture case `Bridge_PromptFormsFixture_OneMintPerMessage` only when P0.2's claude-code prompt-form and head probes pass (otherwise `ClaudeCode_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites`), and, only when P0.2's Cowork hook and bridge probes pass, the same fixtures captured from Cowork (`Bridge_Cowork_PromptFormsFixture_OneMintPerMessage`, `Bridge_Cowork_DequeueTakesHead`); when they fail or are unavailable, A3 instead runs the unsupported-host case `Cowork_P0_2NotPassed_TurnLoggingUnsupported_ZeroMintsZeroWrites`, and the portable bridge cases stay unconditional; the P0.2 outcome that selected the branch is the feature-matrix receipt, `Bridge_UnequalRepresentations_DequeueDeliversHead`, `Bridge_TwoEqualTextMessages_TwoMints`, `Bridge_CrashBeforeAndAfterReplace_OneMint`, `Bridge_RestartReplay_NoReMint`, `Bridge_StalePid_Restarts`, `IdleEnded_ThenMidTurnMessage_MintedAtEnqueue`, `Bridge_ForkedTranscriptWithHistory_NoReMint`, `Bridge_TruncatedTranscript_WarnsNoChange`, `Bridge_DequeueNotHead_Or_PromptNotEnqueued_TurnLoggingUnsupported`, `RootIds_SystemEntryAndUnsupportedSince_SessionEnvelope_AfterWriteAndReplay`, mint-adapter cases `Mint404_BoundMin